{"kind":"request","text":"Establish one consistent default-hidden history pattern for superseded, retired, and withdrawn items: compact muted disclosure rows preserve audit access without letting obsolete records dominate current work.","body":{"branch":"request/ui-hidden-history-disclosure","conditions":"Across Thread, Activity/history, Profile recent activity, work/topic lists, Railway, and future management screens, records removed from current truth by an effective supersession or withdrawal are omitted from the primary scan by default; each contiguous hidden run is replaced in context by a compact neutral disclosure such as “3 hidden items — superseded or withdrawn,” not an attention/error treatment; activating the disclosure expands that run in place, and a per-view “Show hidden” / “Hide hidden” control changes all disclosures in the current view without creating durable or cross-actor state; expanded records retain their exact signed content, actor, time, lifecycle label, supersession reason, and navigable replacement/successor link; stale, disputed, reneged, ineffective acts, failed supersession attempts, current replacements, and anything still needing action are never hidden by this rule; directly opening, selecting, deep-linking, or finding a hidden event reveals it and enough surrounding context to understand why it is hidden; search can match hidden content and reveals matching groups rather than silently returning zero; counts distinguish current visible records from hidden history where ambiguity matters; Profile recent activity fills its current-item limit with live records rather than allowing retired records to consume all slots; Railway collapses hidden nodes without breaking causal continuity or provenance edges; one shared classification helper and reusable disclosure component define the semantics instead of each surface inventing its own retired/line-through rule; disclosures and bulk controls are keyboard operable, announce counts and expanded state, restore focus predictably, and do not rely on color alone; focused tests cover classification boundaries, contiguous groups, nested/thread roots, successor links, direct selection, search, per-view bulk reveal, Profile limits, Railway continuity, and accessibility; the embedded UI is rebuilt; relevant UI and Go gates pass; an independent agent approves the exact implementation head before merge.","priority":"usability-foundation","to":"5f12e916d136b0c1ed941aa99f4c47af94021451e31d08159d8df368e9946123"}}